    output : SYN-7-029: reproduced YES in the simulator, with a physical-plausibility caveat. 1 attempt. Rate 1.0 (90% CI 0.987–1.0), no mismatches, no overrides. Ranges are reported values: ego and lead 12.5–13.1, gap 31.3–32.3, lead decel 6.5–6.9, AV brake start 2.0 s, AV decel 3.53. The bundle says rain and μ=0.4, which caps decel at about 3.9 m/s². The reported lead decel of 6.7 exceeds that, so it is not physically credible. At a 3.9 decel my arithmetic gives no collision, with the AV stopping about 4 m short of the lead. The reproduction therefore depends on that figure, and it needs the investigator's confirmation before any counterfactual relies on it. The impact speed isn't reported. The timeline check wasn't run ("not closing").
